38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: The administrator gap is worse than I feared. Two retire this year, and the last role sat empty for eleven months.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The invoices confirm my fear. Bundled deals held steady, but separate add-ons climbed every single year.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Benjamin"",""self"":true,""raw"":""**Benjamin**: The invoices confirm my fear. Bundled deals held steady, but separate add-ons climbed every single year.""}]}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Benjamin, that yearly climb explains why we keep getting squeezed. We need to lock down the total cost of ownership now.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, precisely. The headline price is a lie; the add-ons are the real bill. We must price the full lifecycle, not just the entry fee.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the empty chair for eleven months is a warning. If we pick a complex system, who actually configures it when the experts are gone?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, that’s the trap. If the system needs constant tuning, we’re buying a permanent vacancy. We need a vendor who stays, not just a license.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Benjamin, @Misaki, your findings align. We need a vendor who owns the outcome, not just the license.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, @Misaki, I found the yard devices are a mess of old models, and the 2021 trial failed because of spreadsheets.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Ryuji, that trial failure mirrors the 2018 pay move. External data lifts always leave us cleaning up the mess for months.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @May, the supervisors dropped the new steps within weeks. If the trainers leave, the system dies with them.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, @Ryuji, the pattern is clear: we buy complexity we can’t maintain. We need a vendor who stays through the rollout, not just the sale.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
