71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Benjamin, D’s on-site engineers solve the maintenance gap. I’m leaning D, but I need to know if it handles our aging yard devices.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @May, D’s engineers stay through rollout. That’s the only option that doesn’t assume we have spare staff to learn it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, D’s on-site team is the only one that doesn’t assume we have spare staff to learn it. I’m leaning D, but I need to know if it handles our aging yard devices.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Benjamin, @May, D’s on-site presence is the only answer to our support chaos. I’m voting D.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, D is built for transport operators. It’s the only one that respects our yard reality. I’m voting D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I’m voting D. It’s the only one that doesn’t leave us stranded with broken data and no one to fix it.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I’m voting D. The on-site engineers are the only way to protect our remaining staff from being overwhelmed.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m voting D. It’s the only option that doesn’t turn our budget into a leaky bucket of endless add-ons.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
